{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01T9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$\\kappa$", "MATH_0004": "$f : \\Spec(A) \\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Spec(\\kappa) \\to \\Spec(A) \\to S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-artinian-finite-type}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:21fb678dd53d41b0c7613fb42d2b95e78ccfa5f01fefae26d176193d47e248a9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e246027c8e60afc9ce4aa0a40ea8075dde301b3445a2fcc018dd248120aef420", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an Artinian local ring with residue field <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a morphism of schemes.\nThen <MATH_0005> is of finite type if and only if the composition\n<MATH_0006> is of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7dc23a1ecd1781829061b3658eebb4d385addd9434fa01cf12a250d21d09145b", "unit_id": "tag:02HV:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01T9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Spec(\\kappa) \\to \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(\\kappa) \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(A) \\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$U = \\Spec(B)$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0008": "$B \\to A$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-composition-finite-type}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-essentially-of-finite-type-into-artinian-local}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:22258ba685b6e87939cc672810f32a6350ce34c3f7235173ee718412123637c2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a5b3a223c76502824aec8c6846b2f4601028bc63ed52991a5b13a49911c8998b", "source_text": "Since the morphism <MATH_0001> is of finite\ntype it is clear that if <MATH_0002> is of finite type so is the composition\n<MATH_0003> (see Lemma <REF_0001>).\nFor the converse, note that <MATH_0004> maps into some affine open\n<MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006> as <MATH_0007> has only one point. To finish\napply Algebra, Lemma\n<REF_0002>\nto <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1ded4a8aa947a6224946776465d8b863a02420a30864a2e25ce36f8814115b88", "unit_id": "tag:02HV:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01T9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$s$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(\\kappa(s)) \\to S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-section-points}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4df9045ab7b9142ac8e71ff232fce99c28796c0c959b032b091afde5b11d67e7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:153ae4848573b7dc63b287939b553c51086b0acf880468a03f73479084556006", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that given a point <MATH_0001> of a scheme <MATH_0002> there is a canonical\nmorphism <MATH_0003>, see\nSchemes, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b1b06b5fb1125fa8a26f304f289efd2bcb53c272b93d0f87ff32aa61757b4a8a", "unit_id": "tag:01T9:prose-0002"}
